/-!
# `EvalRefE0` — sharded kernel check (`catalan-410`, peak-RSS)

The one-shot `decide +kernel` proof(s) in this module each had to materialise the whole of
`LF.sumL (planLits Rm0 Rm0)` — 4 job(s) of products of rational polynomials, their log
forms, `mergeT`, the `logAbsQ 7` enclosures and the final accumulation — inside ONE kernel
reduction. The kernel reclaims nothing inside one reduction, so the peak was the sum of
every intermediate.

The proofs below keep the exported statements byte-identical and split that reduction into
independent kernel checks, each small:

* `jobN_c0` / `jobN_ts` — one check per job, constant part split from the log terms;
* `jobs_eq` / `planLits_eq` — assemble the job literals propositionally (no arithmetic);
* `c0_eq` / `ts_eq` — the `LF.sumL` reduction over literals;
* `merge_eq` — `mergeT` over the literal term list;
* `logN` — one check per distinct enclosure argument;
* `enc_M` — the accumulation with the `logAbsQ` results already verified;
* `enc_eq` — the shared `LF.enc 7` value, reused by every bound in this module.
-/

